WEBVTT

00:00:05.623 --> 00:00:06.916
[rumbling]

00:00:10.086 --> 00:00:11.546
[dragons squawking]

00:00:11.629 --> 00:00:13.339
[people screaming]

00:00:14.507 --> 00:00:15.592
[groans]

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:18.470
What good is having
the king of dragons around

00:00:18.553 --> 00:00:19.929
if he can't keep the order?

00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:22.849
Hey, bud, do you wanna do something here?

00:00:23.016 --> 00:00:24.058
[roars]

00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:26.436
[yapping]

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.938
[whines]

00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:32.108
And where do you suppose
we put these ones?

00:00:32.192 --> 00:00:33.568
Eh, we'll make room.

00:00:33.651 --> 00:00:34.903
-Ah!
-[grunts]

00:00:35.653 --> 00:00:37.822
You brought back a Hobgobbler.

00:00:38.406 --> 00:00:41.117
They're a bad omen. We're cursed.

00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:42.577
[laughs]

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.163
Nonsense. What harm could he do?

00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:49.125
No injuries. They're all a little shaken,
but otherwise healthy.

00:00:49.209 --> 00:00:51.252
Now, who's hungry?

00:00:51.461 --> 00:00:53.713
[laughter and lively chatter]

00:00:56.466 --> 00:00:59.511
Point is, you can't keep bringing dragons
back here.

00:00:59.594 --> 00:01:00.637
Ah!

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:01.721
Come on, boy.

00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:03.306
You're just asking for trouble.

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:05.058
No, you don't, you little thief!

00:01:05.141 --> 00:01:07.393
Those trappers are getting closer
by the day.

00:01:07.477 --> 00:01:09.771
We can handle them. We have the alpha.

00:01:09.854 --> 00:01:11.231
Ain't that right, bud?

00:01:11.314 --> 00:01:13.149
Would you look at how happy they are?

00:01:13.525 --> 00:01:16.486
-She's awesome.
-[laughing]

00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:19.030
Gobber, relax. We did it.

00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:21.991
The world's first dragon-Viking utopia.

00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:23.493
We made the dream a reality.

00:01:23.576 --> 00:01:25.119
Your dream, maybe.

00:01:25.203 --> 00:01:26.788
Mine's less crowded and more...

00:01:26.871 --> 00:01:28.289
[croaks]

00:01:28.414 --> 00:01:30.124
[yelps] ...sanitary.

00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:33.294
Gobber, you're not fooling anybody.
I know you love them.

00:01:33.753 --> 00:01:35.505
[growls]

00:01:36.256 --> 00:01:37.465
[whimpers]

00:01:37.966 --> 00:01:42.262
You're supposed to be the generation
that leads us into the future.

00:01:42.554 --> 00:01:44.764
Ha-ha! Food fight!

00:01:44.847 --> 00:01:48.059
Ooh, gorgeous.

00:01:48.142 --> 00:01:49.727
-Watch the hair!
-Good Fishmeat.

00:01:49.811 --> 00:01:51.771
[makes eating noises]

00:01:52.063 --> 00:01:54.691
Ugh! Thor help us.

00:01:54.774 --> 00:01:57.443
Time to stop worrying
about problems out there...

00:01:57.527 --> 00:01:58.820
-Gobber...
-...and start sorting out

00:01:58.903 --> 00:02:00.196
-the ones right here.
-[grunts]

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.864
[muffled] Okay, okay. I'll think about it.

00:02:01.948 --> 00:02:04.659
Hang up those saddles and get married.

00:02:04.826 --> 00:02:06.077
[chatter stops]

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.245
The "M" word.

00:02:07.328 --> 00:02:09.122
Gross. Unless it's me.

00:02:09.205 --> 00:02:10.248
[grunts]

00:02:10.331 --> 00:02:13.626
Start ruling like a proper royal couple.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.169
Marry him, please.

00:02:15.253 --> 00:02:17.630
You're the only one
with any sense around here.

00:02:17.714 --> 00:02:19.966
With you wearing the pants,
there's still hope.

00:02:20.049 --> 00:02:21.175
-Wow!
-[muffled] Gobber...

00:02:21.259 --> 00:02:22.677
Not awkward at all.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.970
[grunts and coughs]

00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:26.514
-Astrid, don't be like that.
-[chuckles] Whoa.

00:02:26.598 --> 00:02:28.474
That is a definitive no.

00:02:28.558 --> 00:02:31.060
Look, if you need a beard to cry on,

00:02:31.144 --> 00:02:35.189
just lean on my shoulder
and you can cry into my full, thick beard.

00:02:35.273 --> 00:02:38.109
[muffled] Oh, thank you, Tuffnut.
Thank you.

00:02:38.776 --> 00:02:40.278
-So much.
-[clears throat]

00:02:40.862 --> 00:02:42.155
Eret, son of Eret!

00:02:42.238 --> 00:02:43.740
[splutters and groans]

00:02:43.823 --> 00:02:44.824
What's the report?

00:02:44.907 --> 00:02:47.452
Two more trapper barges
spotted in the strait.

00:02:47.535 --> 00:02:48.620
So we go after them.

00:02:49.412 --> 00:02:50.413
What?

00:02:50.496 --> 00:02:54.125
One day, you're gonna pick a fight
you can't win.

00:03:18.483 --> 00:03:19.734
[clicking]

00:03:21.903 --> 00:03:23.529
[growls]

00:03:23.655 --> 00:03:24.906
[guard] Archers!

00:03:26.199 --> 00:03:28.660
[dragons snarling]

00:03:34.874 --> 00:03:36.167
[guard] Deathgrippers.

00:03:40.421 --> 00:03:41.964
[men clamoring]

00:03:45.009 --> 00:03:47.053
[dragons roaring]

00:03:56.771 --> 00:03:57.897
[whines]

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.235
The dragon riders attacked us here,
off the eastern strait.

00:04:02.318 --> 00:04:04.195
[imitates explosion]

00:04:04.278 --> 00:04:06.406
-Ragnar.
-Um, sorry.

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:08.116
My dear warlords.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.078
How go your plans to conquer the world?

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.622
[laughs]

00:04:14.705 --> 00:04:17.375
Grimmel, my old friend.

00:04:17.458 --> 00:04:18.584
-Thank you for coming.
-[roars]

00:04:18.668 --> 00:04:20.586
Oh! [grunts]

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.256
A year since Drago's defeat

00:04:23.339 --> 00:04:27.093
and no further along
with your dragon army, I see.

00:04:27.176 --> 00:04:29.846
You can thank
the young chief of Berk for that.

00:04:29.929 --> 00:04:31.431
Stoick's boy?

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:32.807
Yuck!

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.892
He and his peace-loving dragon riders

00:04:34.976 --> 00:04:38.771
continue to raid our ships
and steal our dragons.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.232
Mmm. That does sound like a nuisance.

00:04:41.732 --> 00:04:44.986
But I'm in the business
of killing dragons, not retrieving them.

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:46.487
[sighs] But, Grimmel...

00:04:46.571 --> 00:04:49.240
That idiot boy has done
all of the work for you,

00:04:49.323 --> 00:04:53.035
gathering the dragons in one place.
Why bother me?

00:04:53.119 --> 00:04:56.831
Because the flock is protected
by a Night Fury.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.211
Not possible.

00:05:02.378 --> 00:05:05.882
[chuckles] It seems
one slipped through your fingers.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.969
Look, Berk's dragons
will follow the alpha,

00:05:10.052 --> 00:05:15.224
so we'll pay you to capture him
and bring the flock to us.

00:05:15.808 --> 00:05:19.312
[singsong] We even have
your favorite bait.

00:05:20.438 --> 00:05:24.525
The only dragon
they left us from last night's raid.

00:05:24.609 --> 00:05:26.110
A female?

00:05:26.777 --> 00:05:29.071
-Hmm.
-[coos softly]

00:05:29.155 --> 00:05:31.949
So, do we have a deal,

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.409
-old friend?
-[clamoring]

00:05:33.576 --> 00:05:35.286
[both roaring]

00:05:35.953 --> 00:05:36.954
[chains snap]

00:05:37.121 --> 00:05:38.247
[guard] Watch out!

